{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01SJRFbMk1fwpPiEop7ueZsi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q13: Chain-of-thought vs tree-of-thought vs graph planning?**\n\n---\n\n**Answer summary** (`03-013-chain-of-thought-vs-tree-of-thought-vs-graph-planning.md`):\n\n| Strategy | Mechanism | Cost | When to use |\n|----------|-----------|------|-------------|\n| **CoT** | Linear scratchpad (\"think step by step\"), single LLM call per step | 1 call/step | Default for all agents — ReAct's \"Thought\" step |\n| **Self-Consistency CoT** | Sample N traces at T=0.7, majority-vote the answer | 5–25 calls | High-stakes factual QA where variance is a problem |\n| **ToT** (Yao et al. 2023) | Beam search over reasoning: generate k candidates → score → prune → recurse | k^d calls (27 for k=3, d=3) | Offline batch tasks only — too expensive for real-time |\n| **Graph DAG planning** | LLM produces a JSON DAG; orchestrator runs independent nodes in parallel | 1 planner call + N parallel tools | ≥5-step structured tasks with known parallelism (LangGraph) |\n\n**Key pitfall covered**: Candidates often say \"ToT is always better\" without quantifying the 27× cost multiplier — or confuse ToT (search over reasoning) with graph planning (DAG of tool-calling sub-tasks)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":310,"cache_read_input_tokens":66891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22237a2f-cd65-4a08-a540-dada4d90eac8","uuid":"1b3b3314-ff08-4525-bfc1-a3ab581a289b"}
